# Copy this file to .env:   cp .env.example .env     (.env is never committed; .env.example is safe to commit.)
# `make run` creates .env for you if it is missing, so copying is only needed to change the options below.

# =====================================================================================================================
# REQUIRED, but you do not type it
# =====================================================================================================================
# TERMINAL_TOKEN is a random secret shared by the web app and the terminal container. `make` generates it into .env
# the first time (`make token`). Leave it commented out here; never put a real value in this example file.
# TERMINAL_TOKEN=

# =====================================================================================================================
# RECOMMENDED: the one line that turns on ✨ AI review
# =====================================================================================================================
# claude in the terminal container, with your own Claude login (type /login in the ⌨ Claude tab once). No API key.
LLM_PROVIDER=claude-cli
# CLAUDE_MODEL=        # optional: a claude model name. Empty means your account's default. (Read only by claude-cli.)

# =====================================================================================================================
# OPTIONAL: what the terminal container may do with your projects folder and your keys
# =====================================================================================================================
# The ⌨ Claude and ⌨ Shell tabs can read AND write ./projects (read-write is the default). Anything that runs there, including
# a peer's code that claude builds, can then change every repository in that folder, .git/hooks included. Set `ro` to make it
# read-only again; claude and the shell then cannot change your projects at all.
# TERMINAL_PROJECTS_MODE=ro
# Where ⌨ Claude and ⌨ Shell work. The default, `live`, is the project folder itself (./projects/<name>): every change they make
# is on your machine at once. `copy` makes them work on a throw-away copy, a scratch space where nothing goes back to the
# project: the safer way to look at code you do not trust. (▶ Run checks always uses a copy.)
# TERMINAL_WORKDIR=copy
# Give the terminal container your ssh-agent so `git push` works there (read by `make`). Off unless set to 1; read the README first.
# TERMINAL_SSH=1

# =====================================================================================================================
# OPTIONAL: use a different AI backend instead. Everything in this block is IGNORED while LLM_PROVIDER=claude-cli.
# Leave it all out if you use claude-cli.
# =====================================================================================================================
# --- A) any OpenAI-compatible server (api.airforce, OpenRouter, Groq, a local Ollama, ...) -----------------------------
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/v1        # required with openai (https, or http only for a local server)
# LLM_API_KEY=                                   # required with openai (not needed for a local server)
# LLM_MODEL=                                     # required with openai
# LLM_FALLBACK_MODELS=model-b,model-c            # optional: tried in order if the main model is down or rate limited
# LLM_MAX_CHARS=40000                            # optional: how much code is sent (default 100000); lower for small models
# LLM_STREAM=true                                # optional: stream the answer (keeps slow gateways from timing out)
#
# --- B) Anthropic's API (a key from console.anthropic.com; billed per use) -----------------------------------------------
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# LLM_MODEL=                                     # optional: default claude-opus-5-5

# =====================================================================================================================
# OPTIONAL: anything else
# =====================================================================================================================
# PROJECTS_DIR=~/42/reviews                      # where cloned projects are kept on this computer (default ./projects)
# SSH_AGENT_MOUNT=/run/user/1000/ssh-agent.sock  # the ssh-agent socket given to the web container. `make` sets it for you
#                                                # (your $SSH_AUTH_SOCK on Linux, Docker Desktop's path on macOS)
